2026 -0600\n\n    spec amendment for #339: criteria depend only on the product, tests/helpers.py and the standard library\n    \n    The spec gate's CI job installs nothing beyond the product, so a criterion that imported a test module (pytest, jsonschema) exited 2 there: the gate recorded 2/2 for every behavioural criterion of #339, #351 and #353, and of #349 before them.\n    \n    Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n    \n    Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01FTZ4RtdkCuPcZHTAMRCQRc\n\n .../criteria/a-claims-write-reads-the-clock-once.sh    | 18 ++++++++++++------\n 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+), 6 deletions(-)\ngit: warning: confstr() failed with code 5: couldn't get path of DARWIN_USER_TEMP_DIR; using /tmp instead\ngit: error: couldn't create cache file '/tmp/xcrun_db-Hv1Geise' (errno=Operation not permitted)\ngit: warning: confstr() failed with code 5: couldn't get path of DARWIN_USER_TEMP_DIR; using /tmp instead\ngit: error: couldn't create cache file '/tmp/xcrun_db-lAgQRRLJ' (errno=Operation not permitted)\n attavo/plan.py                      | 19 +++++++++++--------\n attavo/store.py                     |  9 ++++++---\n attest/records/339/approval-01.json | 10 ++++++++++\n attest/records/339/build-01.started |  7 +++++++\n attest/records/339/spec-02.json     | 28 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++\n tests/test_plan.py                  | 27 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++\n 6 files changed, 89 insertions(+), 11 deletions(-)\ngit: warning: confstr() failed with code 5: couldn't get path of DARWIN_USER_TEMP_DIR; using /tmp instead\ngit: error: couldn't create cache file '/tmp/xcrun_db-1dNZBFdr' (errno=Operation not permitted)\ngit: warning: confstr() failed with code 5: couldn't get path of DARWIN_USER_TEMP_DIR; using /tmp instead\ngit: error: couldn't create cache file '/tmp/xcrun_db-L06SOToh' (errno=Operation not permitted)\n## Problem\n\nClass: fix\n\n`attavo plan claims` reads the wall clock twice for one write. `attavo/plan.py::set_claims` stamps the claim with `now_iso()`, and `attavo/store.py::put` stamps the version envelope with a second `now_iso()`. `now_iso` has one-second resolution, so when the two calls straddle a second the claim's `at` and the version's `at` differ.\n\nSpecimen: lane orange's full run for #336 at 14dc209, under `-n auto`, failed `tests/test_plan.py::test_plan_claims_writes_the_draft_claims_beside_the_order_and_clear_removes_them`, which asserts the two are equal. It passes alone. The test is right; the product is wrong. Root-cause: the clock read is in the product, not the test: one write takes two readings of the time and assumes they agree.\n\nThe change: one plan write reads the clock once. The stamp is taken once per write and used for both the claim entry and the store version, so they agree by construction. No other caller of `store.put` changes its output.\n\nThe stub is thin: it adds the rejection test to `tests/test_plan.py`, red on the stub. The build writes the logic.\n\nRetires: the second clock read in a plan write.\n\n## Claims\n\n- attavo/plan.py\n- attavo/store.py\n- tests/test_plan.py\n- tests/test_store.py\n\n## Criteria\n\n- [structural] the-rejection-test-exists.sh: tests/test_plan.py carries test_a_plan_write_stamps_the_claim_and_the_version_from_one_clock_read\n- [behavioural] a-claims-write-reads-the-clock-once.sh: with the clock forced to a different second on every read, attavo plan claims writes a claim whose at equals its store version's at\n\"\"\"The product's datastore: versioned documents keyed to the tenant.\n\nThe storage ruling (2026-09-25) splits what the product keeps in three:\ngit holds the facts the attestation binds to; this store holds working\nmaterial it does not bind to -- first the Plan's documents -- and never a\nrecord; content-addressed bulk holds the bytes a record points at by hash.\n\nA document is a folder <store>/<name>/ with one file per version,\n<n>.json: {\"name\", \"version\", \"base\", \"sha256\", \"by\", \"at\", \"body\"}. A\nwrite names the version it read (its base) and creates <base+1>.json\nthrough a hard link from a finished temporary file, which fails when that\nversion already exists: two writers from the same base cannot both land,\nthe loser is refused by name, and a reader never sees a half-written file.\nNo database, no lock, and the same behaviour on a mounted folder.\n\nThe store lives under the clone's git common dir, <common>/attavo/store/,\nso every worktree of a clone reads the same store and nothing in it is\never staged; ATTAVO_STORE overrides the location. It is per clone and per\nmachine: sharing across people is the multi-user step, and a hosted engine\nreplaces this module then without changing a caller of get, put or log.\n\"\"\"\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nimport hashlib\nimport json\nimport os\nimport re\nimport subprocess\nimport tempfile\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfrom typing import Any, Callable\n\nfrom attavo.common import now_iso, git_env\n\nNAME = re.compile(r\"^[a-z][a-z0-9-]*$\")\nVERSION_FILE = re.compile(r\"^([0-9]+)\\.json$\")\n\n\nclass StoreRefusal(Exception):\n    \"\"\"A write or read the store refuses, with the reason as its message.\"\"\"\n\n\ndef store_root(root: Path) -> Path:\n    \"\"\"<git common dir>/attavo/store for the clone holding root, or\n    ATTAVO_STORE when it is set.\"\"\"\n    env = os.environ.get(\"ATTAVO_STORE\")\n    if env:\n        return Path(env).expanduser().resolve()\n    run = subprocess.run([\"git\", \"-C\", str(root), \"rev-parse\", \"--git-common-dir\"],\n                         capture_output=True, text=True, check=False, env=git_env())\n    common = run.stdout.strip()\n    if run.returncode != 0 or not common:\n        raise StoreRefusal(f\"{root} is not in a git clone and ATTAVO_STORE is not set\")\n    return (root / common).resolve() / \"attavo\" / \"store\"\n\n\ndef _doc_dir(root: Path, name: str) -> Path:\n    if not NAME.match(name):\n        raise StoreRefusal(f\"{name!r} is not a document name\")\n    return store_root(root) / name\n\n\ndef body_sha256(body: Any) -> str:\n    canonical = json.dumps(body, sort_keys=True, separators=(\",\", \":\"), ensure_ascii=False)\n    return hashlib.sha256(canonical.encode()).hexdigest()\n\n\ndef versions(root: Path, name: str) -> list[int]:\n    d = _doc_dir(root, name)\n    if not d.is_dir():\n        return []\n    found = (VERSION_FILE.match(p.name) for p in d.iterdir())\n    return sorted(int(m.group(1)) for m in found if m)\n\n\ndef latest(root: Path, name: str) -> int:\n    \"\"\"The latest version, 0 when the document has none.\"\"\"\n    vs = versions(root, name)\n    return vs[-1] if vs else 0\n\n\ndef get(root: Path, name: str, version: int | None = None) -> dict[str, Any] | None:\n    \"\"\"The envelope of one version (the latest by default), None when absent.\"\"\"\n    v = latest(root, name) if version is None else version\n    if v <= 0:\n        return None\n    path = _doc_dir(root, name) / f\"{v}.json\"\n    if not path.is_file():\n        return None\n    envelope: dict[str, Any] = json.loads(path.read_text())\n    return envelope\n\n\ndef log(root: Path, name: str) -> list[dict[str, Any]]:\n    \"\"\"Every version's envelope without its body, oldest first.\"\"\"\n    out = []\n    for v in versions(root, name):\n        env = get(root, name, v)\n        if env is not None:\n            out.append({k: env[k] for k in (\"version\", \"base\", \"sha256\", \"by\", \"at\")})\n    return out\n\n\ndef put(root: Path, name: str, body: Any, base: int, by: str,\n        check: Callable[[Any], list[str]] | None = None, at: str | None = None) -> dict[str, Any]:\n    \"\"\"Write version base+1 of name, or refuse: a stale base, an empty\n    author, a body the check refuses, or a writer that landed first. at\n    stamps the version; the default reads the clock, but a caller that\n    already stamped part of the body (e.g. a plan claim) passes that same\n    stamp here so the two agree by construction rather than by chance.\"\"\"\n    if not by.strip():\n        raise StoreRefusal(\"a write names its author (--by)\")\n    if check is not None:\n        errors = check(body)\n        if errors:\n            raise StoreRefusal(f\"the {name} body is refused: \" + \"; \".join(errors))\n    current = latest(root, name)\n    if base != current:\n        raise StoreRefusal(_moved(root, name, base, current))\n    d = _doc_dir(root, name)\n    d.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n    envelope = {\"name\": name, \"version\": base + 1, \"base\": base, \"sha256\": body_sha256(body),\n                \"by\": by, \"at\": at if at is not None else now_iso(), \"body\": body}\n    fd, tmp = tempfile.mkstemp(dir=d, prefix=\".put-\", suffix=\".json\")\n    try:\n        with os.fdopen(fd, \"w\") as f:\n            f.write(json.dumps(envelope, indent=2, ensure_ascii=False) + \"\\n\")\n        try:\n            os.link(tmp, d / f\"{base + 1}.json\")\n        except FileExistsError:\n            raise StoreRefusal(_moved(root, name, base, latest(root, name))) from None\n    finally:\n        os.unlink(tmp)\n    return envelope\n\n\ndef _moved(root: Path, name: str, base: int, current: int) -> str:\n    if current == 0:\n        return f\"the {name} document has no version yet; write it with base 0, not {base}\"\n    env = get(root, name, current) or {}\n    return (f\"the {name} document moved: base {base} is not the latest; the latest is \"\n            f\"version {current}, written by {env.get('by')} at {env.get('at')}\")\n\"\"\"The product's datastore (attavo/store.py): versioned documents keyed to\nthe tenant, outside git. Written red first: on d4c0bc1 there is no\nattavo.store module.\n\nRun: python3 -m pytest tests/test_store.py -q\n\"\"\"\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nimport json\nimport os\nimport subprocess\nimport sys\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfrom typing import Any\n\nimport pytest\n\nfrom attavo import store\nfrom helpers import git, make_tenant\n\nROOT = Path(__file__).resolve().parent.parent\n\n\n@pytest.fixture(autouse=True)\ndef no_store_override(monkeypatch: pytest.MonkeyPatch) -> None:\n    monkeypatch.delenv(\"ATTAVO_STORE\", raising=False)\n\n\ndef test_a_put_from_the_latest_base_writes_the_next_version_and_get_and_log_read_it(tmp_path: Path) -> None:\n    root = make_tenant(tmp_path, \"valid\")\n    env = store.put(root, \"plan\", {\"a\": 1}, 0, \"alice\")\n    assert (env[\"version\"], env[\"base\"], env[\"by\"]) == (1, 0, \"alice\")\n    assert env[\"sha256\"] == store.body_sha256({\"a\": 1}) and env[\"at\"]\n    env2 = store.put(root, \"plan\", {\"a\": 2}, 1, \"bob\")\n    assert env2[\"version\"] == 2\n    got = store.get(root, \"plan\")\n    assert got is not None and got[\"body\"] == {\"a\": 2}\n    first = store.get(root, \"plan\", 1)\n    assert first is not None and first[\"body\"] == {\"a\": 1}\n    assert [(e[\"version\"], e[\"by\"]) for e in store.log(root, \"plan\")] == [(1, \"alice\"), (2, \"bob\")]\n    assert \"body\" not in store.log(root, \"plan\")[0]\n\n\ndef test_a_stale_base_is_refused_by_name_with_the_latest_version_and_its_author(tmp_path: Path) -> None:\n    root = make_tenant(tmp_path, \"valid\")\n    store.put(root, \"plan\", {\"a\": 1}, 0, \"alice\")\n    store.put(root, \"plan\", {\"a\": 2}, 1, \"bob\")\n    with pytest.raises(store.StoreRefusal) as r:\n        store.put(root, \"plan\", {\"a\": 3}, 1, \"carol\")\n    assert \"moved\" in str(r.value) and \"version 2\" in str(r.value) and \"bob\" in str(r.value)\n    assert store.latest(root, \"plan\") == 2\n\n\ndef test_two_writers_from_one_base_leave_one_version_and_one_refusal(tmp_path: Path) -> None:\n    root = make_tenant(tmp_path, \"valid\")\n    store.put(root, \"plan\", {\"a\": 0}, 0, \"alice\")\n    script = (\"import sys; sys.path.insert(0, sys.argv[1]); from pathlib import Path; from attavo import store\\n\"\n              \"try:\\n    store.put(Path(sys.argv[2]), 'plan', {'w': sys.argv[3]}, 1, sys.argv[3]); print('landed')\\n\"\n              \"except store.StoreRefusal as r:\\n    print('refused', r)\\n\")\n    procs = [subprocess.Popen([sys.executable, \"-c\", script, str(ROOT), str(root), f\"w{i}\"],\n                              stdout=subprocess.PIPE, text=True) for i in range(6)]\n    outs = [p.communicate()[0] for p in procs]\n    assert sum(o.startswith(\"landed\") for o in outs) == 1, outs\n    assert sum(o.startswith(\"refused\") for o in outs) == 5, outs\n    assert store.versions(root, \"plan\") == [1, 2]\n\n\ndef test_a_writer_that_loses_the_link_race_is_refused_naming_the_winner(tmp_path: Path,\n                                                                         monkeypatch: pytest.MonkeyPatch) -> None:\n    root = make_tenant(tmp_path, \"valid\")\n    store.put(root, \"plan\", {\"a\": 1}, 0, \"alice\")\n    real_latest = store.latest\n    calls = {\"n\": 0}\n\n    def stale_once(r: Path, name: str) -> int:\n        calls[\"n\"] += 1\n        return 0 if calls[\"n\"] == 1 else real_latest(r, name)\n\n    monkeypatch.setattr(store, \"latest\", stale_once)\n    with pytest.raises(store.StoreRefusal) as r:\n        store.put(root, \"plan\", {\"a\": 9}, 0, \"bob\")\n    assert \"version 1\" in str(r.value) and \"alice\" in str(r.value)\n    monkeypatch.setattr(store, \"latest\", real_latest)\n    got = store.get(root, \"plan\")\n    assert got is not None and got[\"body\"] == {\"a\": 1}\n    assert not [p for p in (store.store_root(root) / \"plan\").iterdir() if p.name.startswith(\".put-\")]\n\n\ndef test_a_body_the_check_refuses_and_a_missing_author_write_nothing(tmp_path: Path) -> None:\n    root = make_tenant(tmp_path, \"valid\")\n\n    def check(body: Any) -> list[str]:\n        return [] if isinstance(body, dict) and \"ok\" in body else [\"no ok key\"]\n\n    with pytest.raises(store.StoreRefusal, match=\"no ok key\"):\n        store.put(root, \"plan\", {\"bad\": 1}, 0, \"alice\", check=check)\n    with pytest.raises(store.StoreRefusal, match=\"author\"):\n        store.put(root, \"plan\", {\"ok\": 1}, 0, \"  \", check=check)\n    assert store.latest(root, \"plan\") == 0\n\n\ndef test_the_store_is_under_the_git_common_dir_shared_by_a_worktree_and_never_staged(tmp_path: Path) -> None:\n    root = make_tenant(tmp_path, \"valid\")\n    common = Path(git(root, \"rev-parse\", \"--git-common-dir\").strip())\n    common = (root / common).resolve()\n    assert store.store_root(root) == common / \"attavo\" / \"store\"\n    wt = tmp_path / \"wt\"\n    git(root, \"worktree\", \"add\", \"-q\", \"-b\", \"lane/x\", str(wt))\n    assert store.store_root(wt) == store.store_root(root)\n    store.put(wt, \"plan\", {\"from\": \"worktree\"}, 0, \"alice\")\n    got = store.get(root, \"plan\")\n    assert got is not None and got[\"body\"] == {\"from\": \"worktree\"}\n    assert git(root, \"status\", \"--porcelain\") == \"\"\n    assert git(wt, \"status\", \"--porcelain\") == \"\"\n\n\ndef test_attavo_store_overrides_the_location_and_a_directory_outside_git_is_refused(\n        tmp_path: Path, monkeypatch: pytest.MonkeyPatch) -> None:\n    plain = tmp_path / \"plain\"\n    plain.mkdir()\n    with pytest.raises(store.StoreRefusal, match=\"not in a git clone\"):\n        store.store_root(plain)\n    monkeypatch.setenv(\"ATTAVO_STORE\", str(tmp_path / \"elsewhere\"))\n    assert store.store_root(plain) == (tmp_path / \"elsewhere\").resolve()\n    store.put(plain, \"plan\", {\"x\": 1}, 0, \"alice\")\n    written = json.loads((tmp_path / \"elsewhere\" / \"plan\" / \"1.json\").read_text())\n    assert written[\"body\"] == {\"x\": 1} and written[\"version\"] == 1\n\n\ndef test_a_document_name_that_is_not_a_name_is_refused(tmp_path: Path) -> None:\n    root = make_tenant(tmp_path, \"valid\")\n    for bad in (\"../x\", \"Plan\", \"\", \"a/b\"):\n        with pytest.raises(store.StoreRefusal):\n            store.put(root, bad, {}, 0, \"alice\")\n    assert not os.path.exists(tmp_path / \"x\")\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
